<title>USA: U.S. interest rates mostly higher in latest week.</title>
<headline>U.S. interest rates mostly higher in latest week.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve announced average interest rates for the week ended April 4, compared with the March 28 week, as follows:</p>
<p>   Federal funds rate.................5.86 vs 5.40</p>
<p>   3-month Treasury bills.............5.17 vs 5.25</p>
<p>   3-month commercial paper...........5.72 vs 5.70</p>
<p>   3-month bankers acceptances........5.60 vs 5.58</p>
<p>   3-month CDs........................5.70 vs 5.65</p>
<p>   3-month Eurodollar.................5.68 vs 5.61</p>
<p>   30-year Government bond............7.10 vs 7.00</p>
</text>
